B7 pre-delivery checks, 2026-11-13 (runs 09:10-15:30 UTC)
Tools: Verilator 5.020 2024-01-01 rev (Debian 5.020-1); Yosys 0.33 (git sha1 2584903a060); sv2v v0.0.12
Final state: every run below uses the delivered sources, except where section 7 says a bench changed after it
(and then the run was repeated with the final bench).

== 0. Portability scans (D30, D36, D41, D45, D53; README Section 2, rules 9 and 10)
Rule 9 in the files B7 adds or changes (casts of a call, field, array element or negation inside an expression or
as an argument; loops without a fixed bound in functions):
  tb/mesh/tests_ctrl.svh:104: loop without a fixed bound in a function: while (cyc + 1 < t) @(posedge clk);
  tb/mesh/tests_ctrl.svh:157: loop without a fixed bound in a function: while (cyc + 1 < t_end) begin
  tb/mesh/tests_ctrl.svh:335: loop without a fixed bound in a function: while (k != CT_KMAX && tries < lim) begin
  -> 3 finding(s) in 12 files
  The three findings are waits inside tasks (time passes in each iteration; the last is bounded by tries < lim),
  not zero-time loops. Before the fixes of section 7 this scan found six casts in tb_sched_ctrl, tb_ctrl_chain and
  tests_ctrl. The older files B7 touches only by @support tags (sink_node, tg_node, run_ctrl) and the older parts
  of mesh_bench and sched_ref still hold such casts; they have given Verilator's counts on xsim since B2-B6.
Empty string parameters: none
Casts of a system function's result (rule 9, D45): none
translate_off/on outside the pragma form: none
Defines of the mesh tops (a define in one file stays defined in every file compiled after it, so all must agree):
