== 7. Findings of the pre-check, all on the test side
1. The rule-9 scan (section 0) found casts that xsim has misread before (README rule 9): int'(call) + 1 and
   CS + 8 + int'(call) in tb_sched_ctrl, int'(ppol) passed to ref_next_kl in tb_sched_ctrl and tb_ctrl_chain, casts
   inside ep_of, ep_t0 and CT05's checks in tests_ctrl. Each now casts into a variable first. No count changed
   (U13 3,358,679 and 419,900; the 4x4 one run 11,075,837, built after the fix).
2. The mutation check (B7_mutation.log) left M16, the clamp after damping, alive: U13's 8x8/2 controller was meant
   to start above K_MAX but took k_fixed(8, 2, 10, TIGHT), which is 12, not 19, and its epoch 0 was not always
   damped. It now starts at 19 and epoch 0 always damps; M16 is killed. U13's counts did not change.
3. U14 +QUICK (40 epochs per network) failed at seeds 2-4 on coverage holes (section 3a). Epochs 1-3 are now
   always the corners (every node at its largest sums, no cross-region demand, one node only). U14's counts
   change: 3,024 to 3,044, +QUICK 407 to 420; 16 seeds pass.
4. While B7 was built: U14 first changed the nodes' latched sums at the falling edge, unlike demand_counter, and
   the least significant bit of the network's sums came out wrong; it now changes them with the tick at the rising
   edge, as demand_counter does. CT03-CT05 first read the plan history one epoch off. Both fixed before these runs.

