== Addendum 14 Nov: after the B7 runs (xsim R-1113-03-01 to 03-10; Riviera-PRO R-1113-U12 to CT01, R-1114-*)
1. U12's stimulus on Verilator. Verilator 5.020 evaluated chance() on the right of && in tb_demand_counter's
   stimulus even when the left side was false (two statements), so its U12 stimulus differed from xsim's while
   every count matched (xsim 8x8/4 at (5, 2): 355 ticks; Verilator 358). Both statements now draw inside an if
   (README Section 2, rule 1). Verilator's U12 INFO lines now equal xsim's (R-1113-03-01) for all seven counters,
   e.g. 8x8/4 at (5, 2): 355 ticks, 12542 samples, 120903 heads, 112537 VCs freed, 225027 flits that must not
   count, 2423 head-and-free pairs (200,000 cycles); +QUICK: 40 ticks, 1567 samples, 15021 heads, 13959 VCs freed.
   U12 seed 1: PASS checks=1,320,015; +QUICK 210,015 (unchanged). Only sim/eda/tb_part5.sv of the bundle changed.
   M01-M07 (the demand_counter mutants) rerun with the new stimulus: all killed (B7_mutation.log).
2. Riviera-PRO 2025.04 EDU (EDA Playground) failed U12 (97,829 errors, R-1113-U12) and U13 (21,631 errors,
   R-1113-U13) on values their testbenches computed: in U12 the model called a head for node 0 local on the 4x4
   counter while the DUT, right, called it cross-region; in U13 sched_ref::ref_next_kl returned 1 for an epoch
   without demand whose plan must stay 2, while the DUT gave 2. A diagnostic U12 with rewritten model forms
   failed the same way (R-1114-U12diag). Compiled with -dbg (Riviera's debug compile, optimizer turned down) both
   pass: U12 210,015 and U13 419,900 checks, every INFO line equal to xsim's and Verilator's (R-1114-U12dbg,
   R-1114-U13dbg). U14 passes without it (R-1113-U14: 420). README Sections 3 and 9.
3. CT01-CT05 do not fit in EDA Playground: CT01's short form (+define+TEST_CT01, 3,629 cycles of the 4x4 design-D
   mesh) was stopped at the 60 s run limit (R-1113-CT01, exit code 137). They pass on xsim with Verilator's counts.
